segments.source:
For example, the solution set of the equation <m>x + 3y + z = 0</m> is a span because the equation is homogeneous, but we would have to compute the parametric vector form in order to write it as a span.
      <latex-code>
          <![CDATA[
\begin{tikzpicture}[myxyz, z={(0cm,0.8cm)}, scale=.75]
  \def\v{(2,-1,1)}
  \def\w{(1,0,-1)}

  \node[coordinate] (X) at \v {};
  \node[coordinate] (Y) at \w {};

  \begin{scope}[x=(X), y=(Y), transformxy]
    \fill[seq4!30, nearly opaque] (-1,-1.5) rectangle (1,1.5);
    \draw[step=.5cm, seq4!50, very thin] (-1,-1.5) grid (1,1.5);
  \end{scope}

  \node[seq4, resetxy, right] at (3.5, 0) {$x+3y+z=0$};

  \point at (0,0,0);
\end{tikzpicture}
          ]]>
      </latex-code>
      (A subspace also turns out to be the same thing as the solution set of a homogeneous system of equations.)

segments.translation:
예를 들어, 방정식 <m>x + 3y + z = 0</m>의 해집합은 동차 방정식의 해집합이므로 생성입니다. 그러나 이를 생성으로 나타내려면 매개변수 벡터 꼴을 계산해야 합니다. <latex-code>
          <![CDATA[
\begin{tikzpicture}[myxyz, z={(0cm,0.8cm)}, scale=.75]
  \def\v{(2,-1,1)}
  \def\w{(1,0,-1)}

  \node[coordinate] (X) at \v {};
  \node[coordinate] (Y) at \w {};

  \begin{scope}[x=(X), y=(Y), transformxy]
    \fill[seq4!30, nearly opaque] (-1,-1.5) rectangle (1,1.5);
    \draw[step=.5cm, seq4!50, very thin] (-1,-1.5) grid (1,1.5);
  \end{scope}

  \node[seq4, resetxy, right] at (3.5, 0) {$x+3y+z=0$};

  \point at (0,0,0);
\end{tikzpicture}
          ]]>
      </latex-code> (부분공간은 동차 연립방정식의 해집합과도 같은 것임이 밝혀집니다.)

segments.source:
It fails the first defining property: <em>every subspace contains the origin</em> by definition.
        <latex-code>
  \begin{tikzpicture}
    \draw[seq4] (-3,-1) -- (3,1);
    \point at (0,-.5);
    \point[red] at (0,-.5);
  \end{tikzpicture}
        </latex-code>

segments.translation:
이는 첫 번째 정의 성질을 만족하지 않습니다. 정의에 의해 <em>모든 부분공간은 원점을 포함</em>하기 때문입니다. <latex-code>
  \begin{tikzpicture}
    \draw[seq4] (-3,-1) -- (3,1);
    \point at (0,-.5);
    \point[red] at (0,-.5);
  \end{tikzpicture}
        </latex-code>

segments.source:
In the picture, one red vector is the sum of the two black vectors (which are contained in <m>C</m>), and the other is a scalar multiple of a black vector.
        <latex-code>
  \begin{tikzpicture}
    \draw[seq4] (0,0) circle [radius=2cm];
    \draw[vector,red] (0,0) -- (2.5,0);
    \draw[vector] (0,0) -- (0,2);
    \draw[vector] (0,0) -- (2,0);
    \draw[vector,red] (0,0) -- (2,2);
    \point at (0,0);
    \point[red] at (0,0);
  \end{tikzpicture}
        </latex-code>

segments.translation:
그림에서 빨간 벡터 하나는 (<m>C</m>에 포함된) 두 검은 벡터의 합이고, 다른 하나는 검은 벡터의 스칼라배입니다. <latex-code>
  \begin{tikzpicture}
    \draw[seq4] (0,0) circle [radius=2cm];
    \draw[vector,red] (0,0) -- (2.5,0);
    \draw[vector] (0,0) -- (0,2);
    \draw[vector] (0,0) -- (2,0);
    \draw[vector,red] (0,0) -- (2,2);
    \point at (0,0);
    \point[red] at (0,0);
  \end{tikzpicture}
        </latex-code>

segments.source:
It contains the origin and is closed under addition, but it is not closed under scalar multiplication (by negative numbers).
        <latex-code>
  \begin{tikzpicture}
    \fill[seq4!20] (0,0) rectangle (2,2);
    \draw[->] (-2,0) -- (2,0);
    \draw[->] (0,-2) -- (0,2);
    \draw[vector] (0,0) -- (1,1);
    \draw[vector,red] (0,0) -- (-1,-1);
    \point at (0,0);
  \end{tikzpicture}
        </latex-code>

segments.translation:
이는 원점을 포함하고 덧셈에 대해 닫혀 있지만, (음수에 의한) 스칼라 곱에 대해서는 닫혀 있지 않습니다. <latex-code>
  \begin{tikzpicture}
    \fill[seq4!20] (0,0) rectangle (2,2);
    \draw[->] (-2,0) -- (2,0);
    \draw[->] (0,-2) -- (0,2);
    \draw[vector] (0,0) -- (1,1);
    \draw[vector,red] (0,0) -- (-1,-1);
    \point at (0,0);
  \end{tikzpicture}
        </latex-code>

segments.source:
It contains the origin and is closed under scalar multiplication, but it is not closed under addition: the sum of a vector on the line and a vector on the plane is not contained in the line or in the plane.
        <latex-code>
  \begin{tikzpicture}[myxyz]
    \path[clip, resetxy] (-4,-2) rectangle (4,2);

    \draw[seq4] (-2,-1,-4) -- (0,0,0);

    \begin{scope}[transformxy]
      \fill[seq4!20, semitransparent] (-1.5,-1.5) rectangle (1.5,1.5);
      \draw[step=.5cm, grid lines] (-1.5,-1.5) grid (1.5,1.5);
    \end{scope}

    \draw[seq4] (2,1,4) -- (0,0,0);

    \draw[vector] (0,0,0) -- (.6,.3,1.2);
    \draw[vector] (0,0,0) -- (0,1,0);
    \draw[vector,red] (0,0,0) -- (.6,1.3,1.2);

    \point at (0,0,0);

  \end{tikzpicture}
        </latex-code>

segments.translation:
이는 원점을 포함하고 스칼라 곱에 대해 닫혀 있지만, 덧셈에 대해서는 닫혀 있지 않습니다. 직선 위의 벡터와 평면 위의 벡터의 합은 직선에도 평면에도 속하지 않기 때문입니다. <latex-code>
  \begin{tikzpicture}[myxyz]
    \path[clip, resetxy] (-4,-2) rectangle (4,2);

    \draw[seq4] (-2,-1,-4) -- (0,0,0);

    \begin{scope}[transformxy]
      \fill[seq4!20, semitransparent] (-1.5,-1.5) rectangle (1.5,1.5);
      \draw[step=.5cm, grid lines] (-1.5,-1.5) grid (1.5,1.5);
    \end{scope}

    \draw[seq4] (2,1,4) -- (0,0,0);

    \draw[vector] (0,0,0) -- (.6,.3,1.2);
    \draw[vector] (0,0,0) -- (0,1,0);
    \draw[vector,red] (0,0,0) -- (.6,1.3,1.2);

    \point at (0,0,0);

  \end{tikzpicture}
        </latex-code>

segments.source:
In fact, it is the line through the origin with slope <m>2/3</m>.
          <latex-code>
  \begin{tikzpicture}
    \draw[help lines] (-3, -3) grid (3, 3);
    \draw[seq4] (-3,-2) -- (3,2);
    \point at (0,0);
    \node[seq4] at (1.5,.7) {$V$};
  \end{tikzpicture}
          </latex-code>

segments.translation:
실제로 이것은 원점을 지나고 기울기가 <m>2/3</m>인 직선입니다. <latex-code>
  \begin{tikzpicture}
    \draw[help lines] (-3, -3) grid (3, 3);
    \draw[seq4] (-3,-2) -- (3,2);
    \point at (0,0);
    \node[seq4] at (1.5,.7) {$V$};
  \end{tikzpicture}
          </latex-code>

segments.source:
Indeed, it is the union of the two coordinate axes, which is not a span.
          <latex-code>
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=3]
  \draw[grid lines, step=.25] (-1,-1) grid (1,1);
  \draw[seq4, &lt;->, thick] (-1,0) -- (1,0);
  \draw[seq4, &lt;->, thick] (0,-1) -- (0,1);
  \node[seq4] at (.25,.25) {$V$};
\end{tikzpicture}
          </latex-code>

segments.translation:
실제로 V는 두 좌표축의 합집합이며, 이는 생성이 아닙니다. <latex-code>
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=3]
  \draw[grid lines, step=.25] (-1,-1) grid (1,1);
  \draw[seq4, &lt;->, thick] (-1,0) -- (1,0);
  \draw[seq4, &lt;->, thick] (0,-1) -- (0,1);
  \node[seq4] at (.25,.25) {$V$};
\end{tikzpicture}
          </latex-code>

열공간은 <m>A</m>의 열들의 생성입니다: <me>\Col(A) = \Span\left\{\vec{1 1 1},\;\vec{1 1 1}\right\}
          = \Span\left\{\vec{1 1 1}\right\}.
          </me>

segments.source:
This is a line in <m>\R^3</m>.
          <latex-code>
\begin{tikzpicture}[myxyz, x={(-.3cm,-.4cm)}, z={(0cm,1cm)}]
  \path[clip, resetxy] (-4,-2) rectangle (4,2);

  \draw[seq4] (-4,-4,-4) -- (0,0,0);
   \begin{scope}[transformxy]
    \fill[white, semitransparent] (-1.5,-1.5) rectangle (1.5,1.5);
    \draw[step=1cm, grid lines] (-1.5,-1.5) grid (1.5,1.5);
  \end{scope}

  \draw[seq4] (4,4,4) -- (0,0,0);
  \draw[vector] (0,0,0) -- (1,1,1);
  \draw[densely dotted] (1,1,0) -- (1,1,1);
  \node[resetxy,seq4,below right] at (1.5,1.5) {$\Col(A)$};
  \point at (0,0,0);
\end{tikzpicture}
          </latex-code>

segments.translation:
이것은 <m>\R^3</m> 안의 직선입니다. <latex-code>
\begin{tikzpicture}[myxyz, x={(-.3cm,-.4cm)}, z={(0cm,1cm)}]
  \path[clip, resetxy] (-4,-2) rectangle (4,2);

  \draw[seq4] (-4,-4,-4) -- (0,0,0);
   \begin{scope}[transformxy]
    \fill[white, semitransparent] (-1.5,-1.5) rectangle (1.5,1.5);
    \draw[step=1cm, grid lines] (-1.5,-1.5) grid (1.5,1.5);
  \end{scope}

  \draw[seq4] (4,4,4) -- (0,0,0);
  \draw[vector] (0,0,0) -- (1,1,1);
  \draw[densely dotted] (1,1,0) -- (1,1,1);
  \node[resetxy,seq4,below right] at (1.5,1.5) {$\Col(A)$};
  \point at (0,0,0);
\end{tikzpicture}
          </latex-code>

segments.source:
Hence the null space is <m>\Span\bigl\{{-1\choose 1}\bigr\}</m>, which is a line in <m>\R^2</m>.
          <latex-code>
\begin{tikzpicture}
  \draw[grid lines] (-3,-3) grid (3,3);
  \draw[seq4] (3,-3) -- (-3,3);
  \draw[vector] (0,0) -- (-1,1);
  \point at (0,0);
  \node[seq4,fill=white, inner sep=1pt] at (-.7,2) {$\Nul(A)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
          </latex-code>

segments.translation:
따라서 영공간은 <m>\Span\bigl\{{-1\choose 1}\bigr\}</m>이며, 이는 <m>\R^2</m> 안의 직선입니다. <latex-code>
\begin{tikzpicture}
  \draw[grid lines] (-3,-3) grid (3,3);
  \draw[seq4] (3,-3) -- (-3,3);
  \draw[vector] (0,0) -- (-1,1);
  \point at (0,0);
  \node[seq4,fill=white, inner sep=1pt] at (-.7,2) {$\Nul(A)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
          </latex-code>

segments.source:
For example, the null space of the matrix
      <me>
        A = \mat{1 7 2; -2 1 3; 4 -2 -3}
      </me>
      is the solution set of <m>Ax=0</m>, i.e., the solution set of the system of equations
      <me>
        \syseq{
        x + 7y + 2z = 0;
        -2x + y + 3z = 0;
        4x - 2y - 3z = 0\rlap.
        }
      </me>
      Conversely, the solution set of any homogeneous system of equations is precisely the null space of the corresponding coefficient matrix.

segments.translation:
예를 들어, 행렬 <me>
        A = \mat{1 7 2; -2 1 3; 4 -2 -3}
      </me>의 영공간은 <m>Ax=0</m>의 해집합, 즉 연립방정식 <me>
        \syseq{
        x + 7y + 2z = 0;
        -2x + y + 3z = 0;
        4x - 2y - 3z = 0\rlap.
        }
      </me>의 해집합입니다. 역으로, 임의의 동차 연립방정식의 해집합은 정확히 그에 대응하는 계수 행렬의 영공간입니다.
